# Artifact Selection

Use the smallest durable artifact that solves the recurring problem.

## Surfaces

- Root rule: short always-on instruction needed in most sessions.
- Skill: multi-step workflow that should be invoked explicitly.
- Docs/runbook: longer reference or setup details.
- Validator script: deterministic check better enforced by code.
- Hook backlog item: timing-sensitive automation that is not safe for manual memory.
- Agent/orchestrator backlog item: specialized context-heavy review that should be isolated.
- Plugin backlog item: reusable capability across many repositories.

## Rules

- Do not promote one-off preferences into durable artifacts unless the risk is high.
- Prefer docs or skills over root rules when the instruction is long or rare.
- Prefer scripts over prose when the check is deterministic.
- Keep capture-mode proposals in backlog only; manual mode is the current allowed scope.

